Summary of conformational results from OPLS-AA for the 36 molecules in the test
set of Halgren et al. See Murphy et al, JCP 1995, 103, 1481 and JCP 1997, 106, 5073.
The only significant problem is for cyclohexanol; this is a well-known artifact of 
AA force fields owing to an overly favorable electrostatic interaction between the
hydroxyl hydrogen and the ring carbons in the axial form - see J Comp Chem 17, 606 (1996).
It can be remedied by making the charges smaller on aliphatic C and H.

